aiṁ yā cakrakramabhūmikā vasatayo nāḍī valīnāmtuyā yā śvāsormi 
maruttaraṃ gagaganoniśvāsakāśāstu yāpākāśodbhava romakūpa nilayā yā 
saṃsthitā dhātuṣu tāndevīripupakṣabhakṣaṇa parāmtṛpyantu bhaktyārcitāḥ ||

<p. 71a> nandantu kulayoginyo nandantu kulaputrakāḥ | 
nandantu śrīkulācāryā ye cānyakuladīkṣitāḥ || 

dehinaḥ sukhinaḥ santu sukhinaḥ santu devavat | 
praśādastu sadānṝṇāṃ caraṇaṃ jīvadhāraṇaṃ || 

vākya uthyaṃ tṛtīya samaya cakradhāya || 

ṅā pālulabhāvātra tarpaṇaṃ || 

aiṁ matsyamāṃsaṃ mahāmāṃsaṃ bhoktavyaṃ janakaṃ caru | 
ṣaṭprakāracaruṃ divyaṃ kubjijuṣṭaṃ namo'stute ||

<p. 71b> jalacaraṃ juhuyāmi svāhā || 

samayaviyatarpaṇaṃ ||

aiṁ jayanti devyāharapādapaṃkajaṃ prasannavāmāmṛtamokṣadāyakaṃ | 
anantasiddhāntamati prabodhakaṃ namāmi cāṣṭāṣṭakayoginīgaṇaṃ || 

yoginīcakramadhyasthaṃ mātṛmaṇḍala veṣṭitaṃ | 
namāmi śirasānāthaṃ bhairavaṃ bhairavīpriyaṃ || 

āpadoduritaṃ rogāt samayācāralaṃghanāt | 
sarvāgimevyapohantu di(*)(?)cakrasyameraṇāt || 

vākyaṃ uthayaṃ cakrapūjā saṃpūrṇārthaṃ dhāya || 

pātrabhokapuya || 

svānako kāyā o svānaviya || 

dakṣiṇākāya || 

nyāsalīnaṃ || 

valivisarjjanaṃ || 

sūryasākṣi || 

śubhaṃ ||

pūrṇam


